Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pi-rp (vendor/pi-rp, git submodule)
  A fork of the "pi" agent toolkit by Mario Zechner (https://github.com/2722550596/pi-rp).
  Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner. MIT License; see vendor/pi-rp/LICENSE.

Worldlines identity client (vendor/worldlines-identity-client)
  The Node client of the Worldlines account service, used to sign in to a
  Worldlines account. Copyright 2026 Ludic Dynamics. Apache License 2.0.

npm dependencies
  Installed by pnpm, each under its own license (MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0 and
  BSD-3-Clause). The optional image library sharp downloads a prebuilt libvips
  binary (@img/sharp-libvips-*), which is licensed under LGPL-3.0-or-later and
  dynamically linked. It is not part of this repository.

Audio
  Platform music, ambience and sound effects under assets/audio/ are CC0 or
  CC BY 4.0 works by third parties. Titles, authors, sources and required
  attributions are listed in assets/audio/CREDITS.md. They are not covered by
  CONTENT-LICENSE.md.

Fonts
  The web app loads fonts from Google Fonts at runtime (Manrope, Caveat,
  DM Mono, LXGW WenKai, Long Cang, Gowun Batang, Noto Sans KR). All are under
  the SIL Open Font License 1.1. No font files are bundled.

Public-domain characters
  "Holmes: The Fourth Case" (templates/whitechapel*) uses characters from
  Arthur Conan Doyle's Sherlock Holmes stories that are in the public domain.
  The plots, text and art are original.
